cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "Explainable Longitudinal Deep Learning for Time-Dependent Alzheimer's Disease Progression Prediction from Serial 3D MRI"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Nhlapho"
    given-names: "Wandile Juddy"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8685-8395"

repository-code: "https://github.com/wawa55/explainable-longitudinal-ad-progression"

url: "https://github.com/wawa55/explainable-longitudinal-ad-progression"

license: "MIT"

abstract: >-
  Reproducible research code for longitudinal 3D MRI analysis of
  Alzheimer's disease progression. The repository contains the controlled
  B0-B2 benchmark workflow, the longitudinal CNN-Transformer M0 reference
  architecture, Integrated-Gradients explainability analyses, component
  ablation analyses, and frozen external validation on OASIS-3.

keywords:
  - Alzheimer's disease
  - longitudinal MRI
  - deep learning
  - 3D MRI
  - CNN
  - Transformer
  - survival analysis
  - Integrated Gradients
  - explainable artificial intelligence
  - external validation
  - ADNI
  - OASIS-3